This afternoon I went to the park to identify the green path issues. 
For the walking path, I started earlier/shorter than the final path and got 1.43 km from the app recording. However, the final path you gave me on April 19[th] says the length is 1.23 km (column "Length"). I used the calculator the compute the real length and got 1.427 km (column "length"). It looks accurate but indicates another issue-- the given path is wrong. The true path should be 1.6 km something (because my recorded path is shorter). You must add more points on the path to achieve accurate length. 

Regards of the biking part, I got a recording of 1.43 + 2.04 = 3.47 km. The given path says 3.229 km, which is also shorter than the recording. You should also re-draw the path to get accurate length. 

So here comes the question: Are these paths make sense? Considering the case of the urban part, 2 km for walking and 4.5 km for biking (you provided wrong length again), both paths are shorter than they should be!

But why cannot we identify this problem from the csv file? Every green phase in the file "ExperimentData_20Apr.csv" is ~20 mins. Take participant 2 for example, the first time stamp for biking green in 16:38, but the first dot on the map is 16:39 (BTW, it started way earlier than the plan, which again shortens the route). It turns out that 16:38 is on the other side of the map.

And it also happened in the end of the route. The last dot on the map is 16:55, and the last time stamp 16:57 is in the middle of the route. In the end, participant 2 only have 16 mins in biking green, 20% shorter than it should be!

As for the walking green part, participant 2 is honest, takes 30 mins to finish. But since participant 3, the same story happens, the last point on the map (stopped early) is 15:18, while the last time stamp in the csv file is 15:20. 

For the early stopping problem, I just noticed you already knew that from the file "map_BikeG_gps.png" you attached in this conversation. For the walking green part, the last person finished the full path is participant 7 (red). As for biking green, none of the participants finished the planned path (gray). 

