Thanks for both emails. Here are my responses and the updated dataset is attached.
1. Data Cleaning
The raw dataset had missing values mainly in Atmotube Left (this we bought after participant 3, so it is blank). Short gaps were filled using interpolation. Regarding the Atmotube PM10 jumping (e.g. P5 BikeU)  --  this is normal behaviour for atmotube as it has an accuracy of +-5 ug/m³ at concentrations below 100 ug/m³ (Atmotube PRO 2 Technical Specifications | ATMO Support Center), which is the case for us:
Metric	Green mean	Urban mean
PM10 (Atmotube L)	3.7 ug/m³	6.0 ug/m³
PM10 (Atmotube R)	3.4 ug/m³	7.1 ug/m³

2. GPS & Route
All GPS coordinates are mapped to the updated route file (ExperimentPath_19Apr.gpkg). Each point shows the nearest point on the route which is more realistic because participants always had a fixed route.

3. Phase Completion
Two columns have been added:
::	PhaseCompletion_pct  --  0 to 100 within each phase
::	ExperimentCompletion_pct  --  0 to 100 across the full experiment per participant
This allows comparison across participants at equivalent stages of each phase, avoiding the time-averaging issue you mentioned.

Please find the updated route and data attached.
Thank you.
Kind Regards,
Pranav.

